ow dangerous  these weapons actually are we meet this  guy inside the police fan which is  rounding up Ever After purgers in  typical Purge fashion this van gets  rolled over that's basically a tradition  at this point in the franchise it  happened in election year and in season  two one tradition they seemed not to  uphold however was having a character  named Sabian then there's this  yes they really did try to make a jump  scare out of literally just a horse  walking LOL then we've got my favorite  guy his name's Kirk  then there are some not so great guys  like this man in a high Vis vast not  exactly great for sneaking around during  The Purge he also uses a mallet as his  weapon even though it seems very easy to  get guns in this world guess this dude's  playing on hard mode as were the  motorcyclists who thought they could  challenge a big truck not a battle  you're gonna win the characters realize  their best bet is to seek Asylum by  crossing the border back into Mexico I'm  not going to talk about the Dracula  Frankenstein and psycho appearances  because they're not even references  they're just there but 99k USD is a damn  good deal for a luxury condo especially  considering inflation by 2049. what a  deal I wonder if you can walk from there  to the festival in Central Park  bettercheck website.com to find out one  of the things I like to do is scan all  of the graffiti in The Purge films and  see if there's anything interesting  written in my video on Anarchy I talked  about how they took a shot at Hollywood  film producer David neustader by making  a man named David newstatter be one of  The Purge victims found in the Street in  this one there's a message that reads  kill David dead there's probably no  connection but if there is wow they're  still not over this are they the mystery  deepens anyway the Native American  Chiago is going to help them get across  the border but not before we stumble  upon a few more eye-opening details  an interesting detai